Rationale (brief):
The run diagnostics and Analyzer both show a clear antagonism between parameter_mean and quality: quality improved (mean 0.123379, best 0.257471) while parameter_mean dropped (mean 0.628024, std 0.021961; decreased ~0.1425 since last iter). That indicates the maximize-parameter_mean objective (weight 0.2) is pulling the search away from higher-quality regions. Removing this objective is the simplest, lowest-risk change to let quality_score drive selection. I therefore propose an objective-level change: drop parameter_mean.

